                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/1075: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-18T17:00:00-03:00">November 18, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 18—3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>295. My 292, November 14, 4 p.m. The President of the Chamber of Deputies, in
                    accordance with constitutional requirements, has just promulgated our trade
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>As soon as arrangements are completed will cable Department for final
                    authorization with respect to exchange of ratifications which will probably be
                    effected by Ambassador Gibson who arrives Thursday morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
